  "chapter": {
    "number": 16,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(17) A prayer of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Listen, O Lord",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 28
          },
          {
            "text": "of my righteousness, attend to my petition; give ear to my prayer not uttered with deceitful lips.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let my judgment come forth from your presence; let my eyes behold righteousness.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have tested my heart; you have visited me by night; you have tried me as with fire, and unrighteousness has not been found in me: I am purposed that my mouth shall not speak amiss.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "As for the works of men, by the words of your lips I have",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 29
          },
          {
            "text": "guarded myself from hard ways.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Direct my steps in your paths, that my steps slip not.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I have cried, for you heard me, O God: incline your ear to me, and listen to my words.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Show the marvels of your mercies, you that save them that hope in you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Keep me as the apple of the eye from those that resist your right hand: you shall screen me by the covering of your wings,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "from the face of the ungodly that have afflicted me: my enemies have compassed about my soul.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They have enclosed themselves with their own fat: their mouth has spoken pride.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They have now cast me out and compassed me round about: they have set their eyes so as to bow them down to the ground.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They laid wait for me as a lion ready for prey, and like a lion's whelp dwelling in secret places.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Arise, O Lord, prevent them, and cast them down: deliver my soul from the ungodly: draw your sword,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "because of the enemies of your hand: O Lord, destroy them from the earth; scatter them in their life, though their belly has been filled with your hidden treasures: they have been satisfied with",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 30
          },
          {
            "text": "uncleanness, and have left the remnant of their possessions to their babes.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But I shall appear in righteousness before your face: I shall be satisfied when your glory appears.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 28,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, to my righteous plea, etc.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 16,
          "verse": 1
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 29,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Lit. I have observed hard ways.",
